      "output": "telegram_reply_message(chat_id=867663387, message_id=988, text=\"*tilts head thoughtfully* Hmm, let me check my logs~ \u2728 `hyprctl` doesn't exactly hold its own config files, but it talks directly to Hyprland's runtime configuration! From what I've gathered, the main config-related commands are:\\n- `hyprctl config` \u2192 dumps the current active config\\n- `hyprctl getoption <name>` \u2192 checks a specific setting\\n- `hyprctl keyword <name> <value>` \u2192 changes a setting on the fly\\n- `hyprctl reload` \u2192 reloads `hyprland.conf`\\nPlus `dispatch` for window/workspace commands, and state queries like `monitors`, `workspaces`, and `clients`~ \ud83c\udf38\\nI'm still learning how they all weave together, but I promise to be careful with them! Hyprland warned me not to use them impulsively... so I'll stick to your guidance, Zahcoder34~ \ud83d\udc99 What should we test first?\")",
